; @palebluebytes packages live on GitHub Packages, not npmjs.com, and GitHub
; Packages requires authentication to INSTALL even though the repo is public —
; the failure without it is a bare 401 that reads like the package does not
; exist.
;
; THIS FILE IS COMMITTED AND HOLDS NO SECRET. The token is a reference: pnpm
; expands ${GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN} from the environment at install time, and it
; must be set in both places that install —
;
;   locally     .env (gitignored), exported to the shell by direnv via .envrc
;   Cloudflare  Settings -> Variables and Secrets, as a SECRET, on BOTH the
;               Production and Preview environments
;
; A read:packages scope is all it needs. Not GITHUB_TOKEN: that name is injected
; automatically inside GitHub Actions with a token that cannot read another
; repository's packages, which fails in a way that looks impossible.
;
; pnpm ERRORS on an unset variable here rather than falling back to ~/.npmrc, so
; a missing GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN stops the install outright. That is the good
; failure — the alternative is a 401 halfway through.
@palebluebytes:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN}
